course: dictionary
lesson: 10539
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean two different things. Capital letters and the words around them show you which meaning is right. «Ulster» with a capital U is a place: one of the four old provinces of Ireland, in the north. Ireland's four provinces are Ulster, Munster, Leinster and Connacht.
explain: With a small u, an ulster is a thing you wear. It is an old-fashioned, long, loose, heavy overcoat, often with a belt and a short cape, worn in Victorian and Edwardian times. «...your acquaintance in the large-pattern leather ulster» tells you the Crocodile is wearing one of these big coats.
explain: Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about a place, or about clothes? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Ulster is one of the four old provinces of Ireland, and it is in the north.
fact: Ulster has nine counties: six are in Northern Ireland, part of the UK, and three are in the Republic of Ireland.
fact: People sometimes say «Ulster» to mean Northern Ireland, but that is not exact, because Ulster has three counties outside it.
fact: An ulster is an old-fashioned, long, loose, heavy overcoat, often with a belt and a short cape.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad dresses like an early motorist, in goggles, a cap, gaiters and an enormous overcoat.
exercise: «The Crocodile was your acquaintance in the large-pattern leather ulster.» What is an ulster here? | A kind of big, bouncy bridge | A river in the north of Ireland | *A long, loose, heavy overcoat | A small boat with oars
exercise: Which of these is one of Ireland's four provinces? | *Ulster | Munster | Wessex | Yorkshire
exercise: In the phrase «the province of Ulster», what kind of word is Ulster? | A sort of motorcar | A type of overcoat | A colour | *A place name
test: «Ulster rugby» is a team name. What does Ulster mean here? | A county in England | A kind of ball | A long, heavy coat worn by a rugby player | *A place, the province in the north of Ireland
test: Toad wears an enormous ulster while he motors. What is he wearing? | A sort of motorboat | A pair of swimming goggles | *A long, loose, heavy overcoat, with a belt and a short cape | A long, loose, heavy overcoat
exam: Lily reads, «He pulled on his ulster and walked out into the rain.» What is Lily wearing? | A pair of wellington boots | *A long, heavy overcoat | A map of Ireland | A cap with a long peak
